-- title:
--   Central vdet = 2, odd and even away units
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $r$ and an abstract $r$-adic frame: a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ that is a discrete valuation ring, an irreducible $\pi \in \mathcal O$ with $\mathcal O$ complete for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, residue ring of cardinality $r$ and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$, together with a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. Further data: a characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, complete for the ideal generated by the image of $\pi$, that ideal being maximal, every element of $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$, every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathcal O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ having a root modulo $\pi$, and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^r \pmod \pi$; and a group homomorphism $v\!\det : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) such that $v\!\det(g) = n$ holds precisely when $\det g = u\,\pi^n$ in $K_0$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^\times$. Let $\bar r \neq r$ be a prime, $N \neq 0$, and $a_1, b_1 \in \mathbb Q$ be such that $a_1 < 0$, $b_1 < 0$ and, for each height-one prime $v'$ of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$, every non-zero element of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_{v'}$ is a unit exactly when $\bar r \in v'$. Let $R_1 \subseteq \mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]$ be a $\mathbb Z$-submodule which is an intersection $\Lambda_1 \cap \Lambda_2$ of two maximal orders with $[\Lambda_1 : R_1] = N$, let $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$ be an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra map, let $v$ be a height-one prime of $\mathcal O_{\mathbb Q}$ containing $r$, and let $\tilde\Gamma$ be a subgroup of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]^\times$ whose members are exactly those of [`CerednikDrinfeld.CosetGraph.awayUnits R₁ v`](def/CerednikDrinfeld_CosetGraphAtPrime.html#L37), i.e. the intersection over all height-one primes $w \neq v$ of the preimages, under the map to $(\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1] \otimes_{\mathbb Q} \mathbb Q_w)^\times$, of the subgroups generated by the local box units of $R_1$ at $w$. Assume finally that some $w_{\mathrm{odd}}$ in that away-unit group has reduced norm $r$. The conclusion asserts three things, with $\sigma$ the induced map on units $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]^\times \to \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ coming from $\iota_0$: there is $z \in \tilde\Gamma$ with $\sigma(z)$ a scalar matrix $c \cdot 1$ and $v\!\det \sigma(z) = 2$; there is $w \in \tilde\Gamma$ with $v\!\det \sigma(w) = 1$; and there is a subgroup $\tilde\Gamma' \le \mathbb H[\mathbb Q, a_1, b_1]^\times$ whose elements are exactly the $x \in \tilde\Gamma$ with $v\!\det \sigma(x)$ even.
--
--   This packages the group-theoretic input needed on the quaternionic side of the Čerednik–Drinfeld uniformisation: the away-unit group $\tilde\Gamma$ attached to an Eichler order in a definite quaternion algebra ramified exactly at $\bar r$ contains a central element of determinant valuation $2$, an element of determinant valuation $1$, and an index-two "even" subgroup cut out by the parity of the determinant valuation. It is used by the fine-moduli statements for the Čerednik–Drinfeld quotient, where the even subgroup and the odd element govern the two components of the uniformising curve.
